comments.body:
@RonnyPfannschmidt would you be able to write up your proposal for what Pytest should look like in the free-threaded future?  Once we have agreement on that, we can work out how to get there incrementally.

For example, I think most people only use xdist to get multi-core local execution, and we could (imo should eventually) obsolete that with native multithreading in core pytest (with a pull-from-queue efficient scheduler).  Then xdist can be multi-computer stuff only, though tbh I think this is usually a mistake and people should do independent runs then combine reports.

But the blocker to all of this seems to be having an agreed list of thread-safety-improving tasks which people can work on!
